    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "This policy could improve public finances if large numbers return to work and reduce the benefits bill, but independent analysts project employment gains far below the stated 2 million target, and the net fiscal cost of tax relief and training is uncosted. Whether the books improve or worsen depends entirely on a parameter \u2014 actual employment return \u2014 that is deeply contested.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the policy delivers employment gains close to 2 million (as stated) or only 60,000\u2013105,000 (as projected by independent analysts) is the decisive fiscal crux: the former would substantially reduce benefits expenditure and raise tax receipts, the latter would make any fiscal gain marginal and potentially outweighed by the cost of apprenticeship tax relief and training.",
